 "_doc": "The Kraken (Pontoppidan, 1752-53): a sea-beast so vast that its back was taken for a cluster of small islands, its arms like the masts of ships, able to pull down the greatest ship. Come ashore: a great mottled mantle with a huge golden eye, propped on thick arms spread over the ground and curling at their tips, two more arms raised high and curling over, pale suckers along them. Built by tools/art/build_gears.py.",
